## 2. `mhdturbFoam` — FOSSEE case-study project

The turbulent variant redistributed here comes from:

> **Rahul Radhakrishnan** (2019).
> *Numerical study of flow of electrically conducting fluid over an airfoil.*
> FOSSEE Case Study Project — CFD with OpenFOAM.
> Vellore Institute of Technology, Vellore, India.
> Developed on OpenFOAM v1812.

FOSSEE (Free and Open Source Software for Education) is an initiative of
IIT Bombay. The upstream `README.md` states that the solver is `mhdFoam` with
"minor changes" and recommends a modified Spalart–Allmaras closure for MHD
applications, citing:

> D. C. Dietiker, K. A. Hoffmann (2003).
> *Modified one-equation turbulence models for turbulent magnetohydrodynamic
> flows.* Journal of Thermophysics and Heat Transfer 17(4):509–520.
> <https://doi.org/10.2514/2.6796>

The turbulent skeleton (`turbulence->divDevReff`, `singlePhaseTransportModel`,
`createFvOptions.H`) and the support headers `createPhiB.H`, `createControl.H`,
`magneticFieldErr.H` and `readBPISOControls.H` are redistributed unchanged from
that project.

## 3. What was changed here

The only differences from the upstream `mhdturbFoam` are the three numerical
corrections listed in `README.md` and detailed in `docs/corrections.md`:

1. restoration of the outer PISO corrector loop;
2. a reference level for the singular `pB` Poisson problem, read from the
   `BPISO` dictionary;
3. `fvOptions` coupling (`fvOptions(U)` and `fvOptions.constrain(UEqn)`) in the
   momentum equation.

Plus the packaging: build files, three verification cases, an integration
example, the verification script and this documentation.

The `channelHartmann` case is a faithful reproduction of the upstream
`mhdturbFoam_model` reference case, including the MHD-modified
Spalart–Allmaras coefficient `Cv1 30` (OpenFOAM default `7.1`) recommended by
Dietiker & Hoffmann (2003) and cited in the upstream `README.md`. That
modification is a dictionary coefficient, not a change to the model code.

## 4. Related solver

For applied fields that are **non-uniform** the full-induction formulation in
this package is not usable; use the quasi-static electric-potential solver:

> W. S. Fonseca. *mhdturbFoamQS: a quasi-static MHD solver for OpenFOAM with
> non-uniform applied magnetic fields.* <https://github.com/wellfonseca/mhdturbFoamQS>
> (ORCID 0000-0002-2602-1964)

